IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pid-dates`
IMPORT `pid-rules`

-- Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) -- the questions of the PERSON WHO MAKES, OR IS THINKING OF MAKING, A PUBLIC
-- INTEREST DISCLOSURE (the whistleblower), and who may suffer detrimental action for it. Each question takes only plain
-- facts (yes/no, dates, a choice from a list); where a question needs the answer of an earlier one (is it a public
-- interest disclosure, does Part 6 protect it), it takes that answer as a yes/no input whose description names the
-- question that gives it (fork F12). The shared definitions, routes, the regulative rule and the penalty table are in
-- pid-rules.l4.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Public Interest
-- Disclosures Act 2012, Version No. 032 (2 October 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published
-- with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance
-- with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 -- the person who makes a disclosure`

§§ `What can be disclosed`

@export Is the conduct I want to report "improper conduct" under the Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 4? It is corrupt conduct; conduct of a public officer or public body, in that capacity, that is a criminal offence, serious professional misconduct, dishonest performance of public functions, an intentional or reckless breach of public trust or misuse of information, a substantial mismanagement of public resources, or a substantial risk to health, safety or the environment; conduct of anyone that adversely affects the honest performance of public functions, or is meant to adversely affect their effective performance and gets someone a licence, appointment, benefit or gain; or a conspiracy or attempt to do any of that. Trivial conduct is not improper conduct.
GIVEN `is it corrupt conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct is "corrupt conduct" as defined in s 4 of the Independent Broad-based Anti-corruption Commission Act 2011 (for example bribery, or a public officer dishonestly using their position)
      `what kind of public officer conduct is it` IS A `Public officer conduct` @desc If the conduct is a public officer's or public body's: which of the eight kinds it is (a criminal offence, serious professional misconduct, dishonest performance of public functions, an intentional or reckless breach of public trust, an intentional or reckless misuse of information or material gained in their work, a substantial mismanagement of public resources, a substantial risk to anyone's health or safety, a substantial risk to the environment), or none of them
      `was it done in their public capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the public officer or public body did it in their capacity as a public officer or public body (answer no if it was private conduct)
      `does it adversely affect honest public performance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct, by anyone, adversely affects the honest performance by a public officer or public body of their functions
      `is it meant to adversely affect effective public performance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct, by anyone, is intended to adversely affect the effective performance or exercise of a public officer's or body's functions or powers
      `did it get someone a gain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that conduct resulted in the person or an associate (a relative, business partner or someone with an arrangement with them) getting a licence, permit or approval, a statutory or board appointment, a financial benefit or property, or another monetary or property gain, that they would not otherwise have obtained
      `could it be a conspiracy or attempt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct could be a conspiracy or attempt to engage in any of the conduct above
      `is it trivial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct is trivial
      `is it for the Court of Disputed Returns` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct can be considered by the Court of Disputed Returns on an election petition under Part 8 of the Electoral Act 2002
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it improper conduct` MEANS
    `s 4 -- improper conduct` (`Conduct facts` WITH
        `the conduct is corrupt conduct`                              IS `is it corrupt conduct`
        `the kind of public officer conduct`                          IS `what kind of public officer conduct is it`
        `the conduct was in the capacity of a public officer or body` IS `was it done in their public capacity`
        `the conduct adversely affects honest public performance`     IS `does it adversely affect honest public performance`
        `the conduct is meant to adversely affect effective public performance` IS `is it meant to adversely affect effective public performance`
        `the conduct got someone a gain they would not otherwise have obtained` IS `did it get someone a gain`
        `the conduct could be a conspiracy or attempt to do any of that` IS `could it be a conspiracy or attempt`
        `the conduct is trivial`                                      IS `is it trivial`
        `the conduct is for the Court of Disputed Returns`            IS `is it for the Court of Disputed Returns`)

-- s 9(1) "a public interest disclosure is a disclosure by a natural person of" information that shows, or that the
-- person reasonably believes shows, improper conduct or reprisal: a definition, JUST FALSE where it fails. s 9(3) "is
-- not a public interest disclosure", s 19(1) "is not a public interest disclosure if", s 20(1) "is not ... if": flat
-- negatives and an "if", JUST FALSE. s 19(2): the written statement "must be given ... no later than 28 days after the
-- disclosure is made"; a later statement is read as not taking the disclosure out (fork F2).
@export Is my disclosure a "public interest disclosure" under the Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) ss 9, 19 and 20? It is a disclosure by a natural person of information that shows or tends to show (or that you reasonably believe shows or tends to show) improper conduct, or detrimental action taken in reprisal for a disclosure. It is not one if it is about a court, an investigating panel or the Special Investigations Monitor, if you state in writing within 28 days that it is not, or if you made it as an officer of an investigating entity doing your job (unless you said in writing at the time that it is one).
GIVEN `am I a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an individual (answer no for a company or other body)
      `what is the information about` IS A `What the information is about` @desc What the information is about: improper conduct by a person, public officer or public body (see the improper conduct question); detrimental action by a public officer or public body against someone in reprisal for a public interest disclosure; or something else
      `how does the information bear on it` IS A `How the information bears on it` @desc Whether the information shows or tends to show that conduct; or, if not, whether you reasonably believe it shows or tends to show it; or neither
      `is it about a court or the Special Investigations Monitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the disclosure is about the conduct of a court, an investigating panel of the Judicial Commission or a member of one, the Special Investigations Monitor or its Office
      `did I state in writing that it is not one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you expressly stated in writing, to the entity you disclosed to, that your disclosure is not a public interest disclosure
      `the day I made the disclosure` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the disclosure
      `the day I gave that statement` IS A DATE @desc If you gave such a statement: the day you gave it (any date otherwise)
      `did I make it in my job at an investigating entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made the disclosure as an officer or employee of an investigating entity (the IBAC, Victoria Police, the Ombudsman, Integrity Oversight Victoria, the Judicial Commission, the Chief Municipal Inspector, the Racing Integrity Commissioner, the Information Commissioner, the Parliamentary Workplace Standards and Integrity Commission) in performing your functions or duties
      `did I state in writing at the time that it is one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether, when you made it, you expressly stated in writing that it is a public interest disclosure, and otherwise made it in the way and to an entity the Act allows
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my disclosure a public interest disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `am I a natural person`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `is it about a court or the Special Investigations Monitor` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `did I state in writing that it is not one` AND (`the day I gave that statement` `is on or before` (`the date` 28 `days after` `the day I made the disclosure`)) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `did I make it in my job at an investigating entity` AND (NOT `did I state in writing at the time that it is one`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `what is the information about` EQUALS `something else` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `how does the information bear on it` EQUALS `neither` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@export By when must I give a written statement that my disclosure is not a public interest disclosure, if I do not want it treated as one (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 19(2))? No later than 28 days after the disclosure is made. If you make such a statement, the disclosure is not assessed as a public interest disclosure and the protections of Part 6 do not apply.
GIVEN `the day I made the disclosure` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the disclosure
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I state that it is not a public interest disclosure` MEANS `the date` 28 `days after` `the day I made the disclosure`

§§ `Where and how to make it`

@export Can I make my public interest disclosure to this entity (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) ss 13 to 17)? Any disclosure may go to the IBAC, the Ombudsman or Integrity Oversight Victoria, unless the Act requires it to go elsewhere: for example a disclosure about the IBAC must go to Integrity Oversight Victoria, one about a police member to the IBAC or Victoria Police, one about a member of Parliament to the Presiding Officer of their House, the Parliamentary Workplace Standards and Integrity Commission or the IBAC. A disclosure about a public service body, a Council or Gellung Warl may also go to that body, and a member, officer or employee may make one to their own body.
GIVEN `whom does it relate to` IS A `Whom it relates to` @desc Whom the disclosure relates to (choose the most specific: a Councillor rather than a Council, a member of Parliament rather than a public service body)
      `whom did I make it to` IS A `Receiving entity` @desc The entity you made, or want to make, the disclosure to
      `do I belong to that entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member, officer or employee of that entity (for a public service body, a prescribed public officer, a Council, or Gellung Warl: a member of the First Peoples' Assembly, a Nyerna Yoorrook Telkuna or Nginma Ngainga Wara member, its Chief Executive Officer or a staff member)
      `do I belong to a Council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member, officer or employee of a Council (matters for a disclosure to the Chief Municipal Inspector)
      `is that entity the one the conduct relates to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a public service body, a prescribed public officer or a Council: whether it is the same body or officer whose conduct (or whose people's conduct) the disclosure is about
      `does it concern a prescribed entity's service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a public service body: whether the disclosure concerns a service, program or initiative provided by an entity prescribed by regulations under s 13(4)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I make my disclosure to this entity` MEANS
    `as an answer` (`Division 2 -- the entity may receive it` (`Route facts` WITH
        `the disclosure relates to`                     IS `whom does it relate to`
        `the entity it is made to`                      IS `whom did I make it to`
        `the discloser belongs to that entity`          IS `do I belong to that entity`
        `the discloser belongs to a Council`            IS `do I belong to a Council`
        `that entity is the one the conduct relates to` IS `is that entity the one the conduct relates to`
        `it concerns a service of a prescribed entity`  IS `does it concern a prescribed entity's service`))

-- s 12(2), (5) and Schedule 2: a disclosure "may be made to a person permitted to receive a disclosure on behalf of the
-- entity"; the Schedule lists them. Not listed: JUST FALSE (fork F5).
@export Could this person receive my public interest disclosure on behalf of the entity (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 12(2) and Schedule 2)? Besides the entity itself, Schedule 2 lets these receive for it: an IBAC Officer, Ombudsman officer or Integrity Oversight Victoria Officer; the Director of the Judicial Commission; a member of the Integrity and Oversight Committee; a police member of sergeant rank or above; the Head of a public service body or Chief Executive Officer of a Council or of Gellung Warl; a person named in the body's procedures; and, if you belong to Victoria Police, the public service body, the Council or Gellung Warl, your direct or indirect manager or supervisor.
GIVEN `which entity` IS A `Receiving entity` @desc The entity you are making the disclosure to
      `who received it` IS A `Who received it` @desc The person who received (or is to receive) your disclosure
      `do I belong to that entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member, officer or employee of that entity (for Victoria Police: a member of Victoria Police personnel)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Could this person receive my disclosure for the entity` MEANS
    `as an answer` (`Schedule 2 -- a permitted person` `which entity` `who received it` `do I belong to that entity`)

-- s 12(1) "must be made in accordance with the procedures established by the entity under section 58"; (3) "may be made
-- orally or in writing"; (4) a written one "must be addressed to the entity or a permitted person and sent (by post or
-- electronically) or delivered to, or left at, the office". s 12A: it may be anonymous. Flat "must": JUST FALSE.
@export Did I make my disclosure in the way the Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 12 requires? It may be made orally or in writing, and anonymously (s 12A), but it must follow the entity's procedures for disclosures, and a written disclosure must be addressed to the entity or a permitted person and posted, emailed, delivered or left at its office.
GIVEN `did I follow the entity's procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made it in accordance with the procedures the entity established under s 58 for receiving disclosures
      `was it in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made it in writing (answer no if you made it orally)
      `was it addressed and sent properly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a written disclosure: whether it was addressed to the entity or a person permitted to receive it, and sent by post or electronically, or delivered to or left at the office of the entity or that person
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Did I make my disclosure in the way the Act requires` MEANS
    `as an answer` (`did I follow the entity's procedures` AND ((NOT `was it in writing`) OR `was it addressed and sent properly`))

-- s 18(1) "is a misdirected disclosure if" (a) and (b): an "if", JUST FALSE where it fails.
@export Is my disclosure a "misdirected disclosure" (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 18)? If you made a public interest disclosure to an entity that may receive public interest disclosures but not this one, and you honestly believed it was the right place, it is a misdirected disclosure, and the protections of Part 6 still apply.
GIVEN `is it a public interest disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your disclosure is a public interest disclosure (see the question "Is my disclosure a public interest disclosure")
      `whom does it relate to` IS A `Whom it relates to` @desc Whom the disclosure relates to
      `whom did I make it to` IS A `Receiving entity` @desc The entity you made the disclosure to
      `do I belong to that entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member, officer or employee of that entity
      `do I belong to a Council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member, officer or employee of a Council
      `is that entity the one the conduct relates to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a public service body, a prescribed public officer or a Council: whether it is the body or officer the disclosure is about
      `does it concern a prescribed entity's service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a public service body: whether it concerns a service of an entity prescribed under s 13(4)
      `did I honestly believe it was the right place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you honestly believed the entity was an appropriate one to make the disclosure to
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my disclosure a misdirected disclosure` MEANS
    `as an answer` (    `is it a public interest disclosure`
                    AND (NOT (`Division 2 -- the entity may receive it` (`Route facts` WITH
                            `the disclosure relates to`                     IS `whom does it relate to`
                            `the entity it is made to`                      IS `whom did I make it to`
                            `the discloser belongs to that entity`          IS `do I belong to that entity`
                            `the discloser belongs to a Council`            IS `do I belong to a Council`
                            `that entity is the one the conduct relates to` IS `is that entity the one the conduct relates to`
                            `it concerns a service of a prescribed entity`  IS `does it concern a prescribed entity's service`)))
                    AND `is a Division 2 entity` `whom did I make it to`
                    AND `did I honestly believe it was the right place`)

§§ `After the disclosure: notification, advice and assessment`

@export By when must the entity I disclosed to notify my disclosure for assessment and tell me in writing what it has done (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) ss 21(2), 24(4))? Both no later than 28 days after the disclosure is made to it.
GIVEN `the day I made the disclosure` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the disclosure to the entity
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the entity notify my disclosure and tell me` MEANS `the date` 28 `days after` `the day I made the disclosure`

-- s 24 applies to a disclosure "referred to in section 21(1)(a)" (made under Division 2 to an entity other than the IBAC,
-- or Integrity Oversight Victoria or the Committee under s 14, or misdirected) and to a police complaint disclosure.
-- (2) if notified, the entity must advise; (3) if not, it must advise, but (5) only if the person "has indicated ... or
-- it otherwise appears ... that the person wishes to receive the protections". s 12A(2): no duty for an anonymous
-- discloser. The duty is the regulative rule in pid-rules.l4, run here by trace. Where s 24 puts no duty: the answer
-- says so.
@export Has the entity I made my disclosure to told me in writing, in time, whether it notified my disclosure for assessment (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 24)? An entity other than the IBAC (or Integrity Oversight Victoria or the Integrity and Oversight Committee receiving under s 14) must advise you in writing within 28 days whether it notified your disclosure to the IBAC, Integrity Oversight Victoria or the Integrity and Oversight Committee for assessment. If it did not notify it, it must tell you only if you indicated, or it appears, that you want the Act's protections. No advice is owed if you disclosed anonymously.
GIVEN `did I make it to an entity s 24 covers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made it to an entity other than the IBAC (and other than to Integrity Oversight Victoria or the Integrity and Oversight Committee for a disclosure the Act requires to go to them), including a misdirected disclosure; or, as a police officer or protective services officer, made a police complaint disclosure to the Chief Commissioner of Police
      `did I make it anonymously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made the disclosure anonymously
      `was it notified for assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity notified your disclosure for assessment (answer no if it has not, or you do not know)
      `did I indicate I want the protections` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you indicated to the entity, or it otherwise appeared to it, that you wish to receive the protections the Act gives a public interest disclosure
      `the day I made the disclosure` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the disclosure to the entity
      `have I been advised in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity has given you its advice in writing
      `the day I was advised` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day it gave you the written advice (any date otherwise)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty to advise me`
`Has the entity told me in time` MEANS
    IF (NOT `did I make it to an entity s 24 covers`) OR `did I make it anonymously` OR ((NOT `was it notified for assessment`) AND (NOT `did I indicate I want the protections`))
    THEN `the Act puts no duty to advise me on these facts`
    ELSE `what became of the duty to advise` 28 `have I been advised in writing` (`the days from` `the day I made the disclosure` `to` `the day I was advised`) (`the days from` `the day I made the disclosure` `to` `today`)

-- s 26(5): "the IBAC may determine that a disclosure which has been notified to the IBAC under section 21 or 22 is not a
-- public interest complaint if" it considers another body should deal, or has dealt, with it; (6) "Before determining
-- ... the IBAC must (a) consult with the notifying entity; and (b) unless the disclosure was made anonymously, obtain the
-- consent of the person". A disclosure made to the IBAC directly is outside (5), and s 26(3)(a) then requires a public
-- interest complaint determination where the disclosure shows improper conduct: JUST FALSE (fork F6). A precondition not
-- met: JUST FALSE (fork F7). Applied also to Integrity Oversight Victoria and the Committee? No: ss 31(5) and 31B(5)
-- apply only ss 27 to 30, not s 26(5) (finding 7).
@export Can the IBAC decide that my disclosure is not a public interest complaint because another body should deal with it, or already has (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 26(5) and (6))? Only for a disclosure notified to the IBAC by another entity, only after the IBAC has consulted that entity, and, unless you disclosed anonymously, only with your consent.
GIVEN `was it notified to the IBAC by another entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity you disclosed to (or the Chief Commissioner of Police) notified your disclosure to the IBAC under s 21 or 22 (answer no if you made it to the IBAC yourself)
      `does the IBAC consider another body should deal with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the IBAC considers it more appropriate for the notifying entity or another public body to deal with the matter, or that the matter has been adequately dealt with by such a body as required by law or under an enterprise agreement under the Fair Work Act 2009
      `has the IBAC consulted the notifying entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the IBAC has consulted the entity that notified the disclosure
      `did I make it anonymously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made the disclosure anonymously
      `have I consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have consented to the disclosure being dealt with other than as a public interest complaint
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the IBAC send my disclosure elsewhere` MEANS
    `as an answer` (    `was it notified to the IBAC by another entity`
                    AND `does the IBAC consider another body should deal with it`
                    AND `has the IBAC consulted the notifying entity`
                    AND (`did I make it anonymously` OR `have I consented`))

§§ `Protection under Part 6`

-- s 38(1) "This Part applies to the following disclosures" (a) to (d): a list not closed with "only"; none of them is
-- NOTHING-kind *open list* (other law may protect the person, s 7).
@export Do the protections of Part 6 of the Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) apply to my disclosure (s 38)? They apply from the time it is made, whether or not it is notified or found to be a public interest complaint, to a public interest disclosure made to an entity that may receive it and in the way the Act requires, to a misdirected disclosure, to a police officer's complaint about another officer under s 167(3) of the Victoria Police Act 2013, and to an external disclosure made as s 38A allows. Further information you give the same bodies is protected too.
GIVEN `is it a public interest disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your disclosure is a public interest disclosure (see the question "Is my disclosure a public interest disclosure")
      `may that entity receive it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made it to an entity that may or must receive it (see the question "Can I make my disclosure to this entity")
      `did I make it in the required way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made it following the entity's procedures and, if in writing, addressed and sent properly (see the question "Did I make my disclosure in the way the Act requires")
      `is it a misdirected disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a misdirected disclosure (see the question "Is my disclosure a misdirected disclosure")
      `is it a police complaint under s 167(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a complaint you made, as a police officer or protective services officer, about another police officer or protective services officer under s 167(3) of the Victoria Police Act 2013
      `is it an external disclosure the Act allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is an external disclosure made as s 38A allows (see the question "Can I make an external disclosure")
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does Part 6 protect my disclosure` MEANS
    IF    (`is it a public interest disclosure` AND `may that entity receive it` AND `did I make it in the required way`)
       OR (`is it a public interest disclosure` AND `is it a misdirected disclosure`)
       OR `is it a police complaint under s 167(3)`
       OR (`is it a public interest disclosure` AND `is it an external disclosure the Act allows`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (open list: s 38(1); s 7 keeps other protections)

-- s 38A(1) "An external disclosure is a public interest disclosure made to a person or body who is not an entity to whom
-- a public interest disclosure may be made under Division 2"; (2) "is made in accordance with this section if" (a) to
-- (d); (5) "is not ... made in accordance with this section if": a definition, an "if" and a flat negative, so JUST
-- FALSE where they fail. The periods are fixed in the text's own words (6 months, 30 days, 12 months); a condition
-- "has not been notified ... within 6 months" is met only once the 6 months have run (fork F8). The request for advice
-- may be made at any time (fork F9); in (4)(c)(ii) "within 6 months after that response" is read with "advised" (fork F10).
@export Can I make an "external disclosure" to someone outside the integrity system, such as a journalist or member of Parliament, and keep the Act's protections (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 38A)? Only if your original disclosure, made under the Act and not anonymously, was determined to be a public interest complaint and you were told so; the external one is on substantially the same matter; and either (a) you were told of no action within 6 months of that notice and got no answer within 30 days to a request for progress, or (b) the investigation was not completed within 12 months of that notice, you asked for progress, and you got no answer within 30 days, or an answer that it was still ongoing but no advice of completion within 6 months after it. It must not contain information that may prejudice a criminal investigation or legal proceeding you know of, or reveal IBAC or police investigative methods.
GIVEN `is the recipient an entity under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person or body you are disclosing to is one to which a public interest disclosure may be made under Division 2 of Part 2 (such as the IBAC, the Ombudsman, Integrity Oversight Victoria or your own public service body); if so, it is not an external disclosure
      `did I make an original disclosure under the Act, not anonymously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you previously made a public interest disclosure in the way and to an entity the Act allows, and not anonymously
      `was it determined a public interest complaint and was I told` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that original disclosure was determined (by the IBAC, Integrity Oversight Victoria or the Integrity and Oversight Committee) to be a public interest complaint, and you were notified of that determination
      `the day I was told of the determination` IS A DATE @desc The day you were notified that the original disclosure was determined to be a public interest complaint
      `is it substantially the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the subject matter of the external disclosure is substantially the same as that of the original disclosure
      `have I been told of any action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the investigating entity has notified you of any action taken on the original disclosure
      `the day I was first told of action` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day it first notified you of action taken (any date otherwise)
      `did I ask for progress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you requested advice on the progress of the public interest complaint from the investigating entity
      `the day I asked` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day you made the request (any date otherwise)
      `did I get a response` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have received a response to that request
      `the day of the response` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day you received the response (any date otherwise)
      `did the response say it is ongoing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the response advised that the investigation is still ongoing
      `has the investigation been completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the investigation of the public interest complaint has been completed
      `the day it was completed` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day it was completed (any date otherwise)
      `have I been told it is completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been advised that the investigation has been completed
      `the day I was told it is completed` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day you were so advised (any date otherwise)
      `the day of the external disclosure` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or made) the external disclosure
      `may it prejudice a proceeding I know of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it contains information that may prejudice a criminal investigation, criminal proceeding or other legal proceeding of which you are aware
      `may it reveal an investigative method` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it contains information likely to lead to the disclosure of an investigative method used by the IBAC or Victoria Police
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I make an external disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `is the recipient an entity under the Act` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `may it prejudice a proceeding I know of` OR `may it reveal an investigative method` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT (`did I make an original disclosure under the Act, not anonymously` AND `was it determined a public interest complaint and was I told` AND `is it substantially the same matter`)) THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE `as an answer` (`s 38A(3)` OR `s 38A(4)`)
    WHERE
        `six months on` MEANS `the date` 6 `months after` `the day I was told of the determination`
        `twelve months on` MEANS `the date` 12 `months after` `the day I was told of the determination`
        `thirty days after the request` MEANS `the date` 30 `days after` `the day I asked`
        `six months after the response` MEANS `the date` 6 `months after` `the day of the response`
        `ext` MEANS `the day of the external disclosure`
        `no action notified within 6 months` MEANS
                (`ext` `is after` `six months on`)
            AND ((NOT `have I been told of any action`) OR (`the day I was first told of action` `is after` `six months on`))
        `no response within 30 days` MEANS
                `did I ask for progress`
            AND (`ext` `is after` `thirty days after the request`)
            AND ((NOT `did I get a response`) OR (`the day of the response` `is after` `thirty days after the request`))
        `not completed within 12 months` MEANS
                (`ext` `is after` `twelve months on`)
            AND ((NOT `has the investigation been completed`) OR (`the day it was completed` `is after` `twelve months on`))
        `an ongoing response within 30 days` MEANS
                `did I ask for progress`
            AND `did I get a response`
            AND (`the day of the response` `is on or before` `thirty days after the request`)
            AND `did the response say it is ongoing`
        `no completion advice within 6 months of it` MEANS
                (`ext` `is after` `six months after the response`)
            AND ((NOT `have I been told it is completed`) OR (`the day I was told it is completed` `is after` `six months after the response`))
        `s 38A(3)` MEANS `no action notified within 6 months` AND `no response within 30 days`
        `s 38A(4)` MEANS
                `not completed within 12 months`
            AND `did I ask for progress`
            AND (`no response within 30 days` OR (`an ongoing response within 30 days` AND `no completion advice within 6 months of it`))

-- ss 39(1), 40(1), 41(1) give the immunity, the confidentiality release and absolute privilege; (2) of each: "does not
-- apply to a person who ... has contravened section 72(1) or (2)": flat negative, JUST FALSE. s 42: "a person's
-- liability for his or her own conduct is not affected": JUST FALSE. Where Part 6 does not apply the Act gives nothing:
-- NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording* (s 7: other law may still protect).
DECLARE `Kind of liability` IS ONE OF
    `civil, criminal or administrative liability, including discipline, for making the disclosure`
    `an offence or breach of a duty of confidentiality, an oath or an agreement, for making the disclosure`
    `an action for defamation over the disclosure`
    `liability for my own conduct that I disclosed`

@export Am I protected from this liability for making my disclosure (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) ss 39 to 42)? If Part 6 applies, you are not subject to civil, criminal or administrative (including disciplinary) liability for making the disclosure; you do not commit an offence or breach a duty of confidentiality, oath or agreement by making it; and you have absolute privilege against defamation. None of this applies if you knowingly gave false or misleading information (s 72), and your liability for your own conduct is not affected by disclosing it.
GIVEN `which liability` IS A `Kind of liability` @desc The kind of liability you are concerned about
      `does Part 6 apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Part 6 applies to your disclosure (see the question "Do the protections of Part 6 apply to my disclosure")
      `did I knowingly give false information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in making the disclosure, you gave information you knew was false or misleading in a material particular, contrary to s 72(1) or (2)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I protected from this liability` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `which liability` EQUALS `liability for my own conduct that I disclosed` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `does Part 6 apply`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 38; s 7)
           IF `did I knowingly give false information` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Detrimental action in reprisal -- if something has been done or threatened against you`

@export Is what was done or threatened against me "detrimental action in reprisal" for a public interest disclosure (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) ss 3 and 43)? Detrimental action includes action causing injury, loss or damage; intimidation or harassment; and discrimination, disadvantage or adverse treatment in your employment, career, profession, trade or business, including discipline. It is in reprisal if it was taken or threatened (or someone was incited or permitted to take or threaten it) because, or in the belief that, you or anyone else made or intends to make the disclosure, or cooperated or intends to cooperate with an investigation of it. It is not if you made the disclosure and knowingly gave false information (s 72).
GIVEN `what was done or threatened` IS A `Kind of action` @desc What was done or threatened against you
      `does Part 6 protect the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Part 6 applies to the disclosure (made or intended) that the action is about (see the question "Do the protections of Part 6 apply to my disclosure")
      `was a disclosure or cooperation a reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reason for the action was that you or anyone else made or intends to make the disclosure, or cooperated or intends to cooperate with an investigation of it (or a belief that this was so)
      `did I make the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person who made the disclosure
      `did I knowingly give false information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in making it, you gave information you knew was false or misleading in a material particular (s 72)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it detrimental action in reprisal` MEANS
    `s 43 -- detrimental action in reprisal` (`Reprisal facts` WITH
        `the kind of action taken or threatened`                         IS `what was done or threatened`
        `the disclosure is one Part 6 protects`                          IS `does Part 6 protect the disclosure`
        `a reason was a disclosure or cooperation with an investigation` IS `was a disclosure or cooperation a reason`
        `the person treated so made the disclosure`                      IS `did I make the disclosure`
        `that person contravened s 72 in making it`                      IS `did I knowingly give false information`)

-- s 44(2): "A manager may take management action that is detrimental action ... only if the fact that the employee has
-- made the public interest disclosure is not a reason": "only if", JUST FALSE where the disclosure is a reason. (3)
-- lists management action ("includes"); action outside the list is still management action if it is one.
@export May my manager take this management action against me after my disclosure (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 44)? A manager may still take management action (performance development and training, conditions of employment, discipline, workplace safety), even if it is detrimental, but only if the fact that you made the disclosure is not a reason for it.
GIVEN `is it management action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is management action by your manager, such as action about performance development (including training), conditions of employment, discipline, or the safety of the workplace
      `is my disclosure a reason for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fact that you made the public interest disclosure is a reason for the manager taking the action
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May my manager take this action` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `is it management action`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 44 speaks only of management action)
           IF `is my disclosure a reason for it` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 45(1) the offence; (2) the defence that no s 43(1)(a) reason was a reason (the same test as s 43); (3) the defence
-- that the disclosure was determined not to be a public interest complaint and the person knew it when acting; (4) not
-- if that determination was under s 26(5). A defence made out: no offence, JUST FALSE.
@export Is it an offence to take this action against me (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 45)? Taking detrimental action in reprisal for a public interest disclosure is an offence (up to 240 penalty units or 2 years' imprisonment or both). It is a defence that the disclosure was not a reason, or that the IBAC, Integrity Oversight Victoria or the Integrity and Oversight Committee had determined that the disclosure is not a public interest complaint and the person knew it when acting (but not where the determination was that another body should deal with it, s 26(5)).
GIVEN `what was done or threatened` IS A `Kind of action` @desc What was done or threatened against you
      `does Part 6 protect the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Part 6 applies to the disclosure the action is about
      `was a disclosure or cooperation a reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reason for the action was that you or anyone else made or intends to make the disclosure, or cooperated or intends to cooperate with an investigation
      `did I make the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person who made the disclosure
      `did I knowingly give false information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in making it, you gave information you knew was false or misleading (s 72)
      `was it determined not a public interest complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the IBAC, Integrity Oversight Victoria or the Integrity and Oversight Committee had determined that the disclosure is not a public interest complaint
      `did the person know of that when acting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who took the action knew of that determination at the time
      `was that because another body should deal with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the determination was made under s 26(5) (another body should deal, or has adequately dealt, with the matter)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it an offence to take this action against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Is it detrimental action in reprisal` `what was done or threatened` `does Part 6 protect the disclosure` `was a disclosure or cooperation a reason` `did I make the disclosure` `did I knowingly give false information`
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        IF x
        THEN `as an answer` (NOT (`was it determined not a public interest complaint` AND `did the person know of that when acting` AND (NOT `was that because another body should deal with it`)))
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (carried from s 43: limited by its own wording, or the open list of s 3)

-- s 46(1): "If a person is convicted or found guilty of an offence against section 45, the court may ... order ...
-- damages"; (2) "If (a) the employer of a person; or (b) someone in the course of employment with, or while acting as an
-- agent of, the employer ... is convicted", the court may order reinstatement or re-employment.
DECLARE `What the court may order on conviction` IS ONE OF
    `nothing under s 46: no one has been convicted or found guilty`
    `damages for my injury, loss or damage`
    `damages, and that my employer reinstate or re-employ me`

@export If someone is convicted of taking reprisal action against me, what can the court order for me (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 46)? On a conviction or finding of guilt under s 45 the court may order the offender to pay you damages for injury, loss or damage within a time it sets; and if the offender is your employer, or someone acting for or employed by your employer, it may also order that your employer reinstate or re-employ you in your former position or a similar one.
GIVEN `has someone been convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person has been convicted or found guilty of an offence against s 45 for detrimental action taken against you
      `is the offender my employer or acting for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person convicted is your employer, or someone who was in the course of employment with, or acting as an agent of, your employer
GIVETH A `What the court may order on conviction`
`What can the court order on conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `has someone been convicted`) THEN `nothing under s 46: no one has been convicted or found guilty`
           IF `is the offender my employer or acting for it` THEN `damages, and that my employer reinstate or re-employ me`
           OTHERWISE `damages for my injury, loss or damage`

-- s 47(1): the person who takes detrimental action in reprisal "is liable in damages for any injury, loss or damage";
-- (5) even without a prosecution. With no injury, loss or damage the Act says nothing of what is recovered (exemplary
-- damages under (3) are a court's remedy): NOTHING-kind *silent*.
@export Can I sue for damages for the reprisal (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 47)? A person who takes detrimental action against you in reprisal for a public interest disclosure is liable to you in damages for any injury, loss or damage, recoverable as for a tort in any court with jurisdiction, with any tort remedy including exemplary damages, whether or not they have been prosecuted.
GIVEN `what was done or threatened` IS A `Kind of action` @desc What was done or threatened against you
      `does Part 6 protect the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Part 6 applies to the disclosure the action is about
      `was a disclosure or cooperation a reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reason for the action was that you or anyone else made or intends to make the disclosure, or cooperated or intends to cooperate with an investigation
      `did I make the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person who made the disclosure
      `did I knowingly give false information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in making it, you gave information you knew was false or misleading (s 72)
      `did I suffer injury, loss or damage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered injury, loss or damage from the action
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I sue for damages for the reprisal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Is it detrimental action in reprisal` `what was done or threatened` `does Part 6 protect the disclosure` `was a disclosure or cooperation a reason` `did I make the disclosure` `did I knowingly give false information`
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        IF x
        THEN IF `did I suffer injury, loss or damage` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: no loss)
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (carried from s 43)

-- s 48(1): "If a person in the course of employment with, or while acting as an agent of, a public body takes
-- detrimental action ... the public body and the employee or agent ... are jointly and severally civilly liable"; (2)
-- "It is a defence ... if the public body proves ... that it took reasonable precautions". An "if", and a defence made
-- out: JUST FALSE.
@export Can I also sue the public body whose employee or agent took the reprisal action (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 48)? If the person acted in the course of employment with, or as an agent of, a public body, the body and the person are jointly and severally liable and you may sue either or both, unless the body proves it took reasonable precautions to prevent the reprisal.
GIVEN `is it detrimental action in reprisal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action is detrimental action in reprisal for a public interest disclosure (see the question "Is it detrimental action in reprisal")
      `did they act for a public body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who took the action did so in the course of employment with, or while acting as an agent of, a public body
      `did the body take reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the public body proves, on the balance of probabilities, that it took reasonable precautions to prevent the employee or agent from taking reprisal action against you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I also sue the public body` MEANS
    `as an answer` (`is it detrimental action in reprisal` AND `did they act for a public body` AND (NOT `did the body take reasonable precautions`))

-- s 47(7): "costs against the person alleging that detrimental action has been taken in reprisal ... must not be awarded
-- unless the court is satisfied" the claim is vexatious or the person did not conduct the litigation reasonably. Once
-- the "unless" is met the court's ordinary discretion returns: JUST TRUE ("can") (fork F11).
@export Can I be ordered to pay costs in my damages claim for reprisal (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 47(7))? Costs must not be awarded against you unless the court is satisfied that your claim that detrimental action occurred is vexatious, or that you did not conduct the litigation reasonably.
GIVEN `is my claim vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that your claim that detrimental action occurred is vexatious
      `did I conduct the litigation unreasonably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that you did not conduct the litigation reasonably
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be ordered to pay costs` MEANS `as an answer` (`is my claim vexatious` OR `did I conduct the litigation unreasonably`)

-- s 50(a): an application "may be made by (a) a person who believes that detrimental action has been taken or may be
-- taken against him or her in reprisal for a public interest disclosure". A list of applicants not closed with "only":
-- NOTHING where the person does not hold the belief.
@export Can I apply to the Supreme Court for an injunction or an order to remedy reprisal action (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) ss 49 and 50)? If you believe detrimental action has been taken or may be taken against you in reprisal for a public interest disclosure, you may apply; if satisfied, the Court may order the person to remedy the action or grant an injunction, including on an interim basis.
GIVEN `do I believe reprisal action has been or may be taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you believe that detrimental action has been taken, or may be taken, against you in reprisal for a public interest disclosure
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply to the Supreme Court` MEANS
    IF `do I believe reprisal action has been or may be taken` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 50(a))

DECLARE `My employer` IS ONE OF
    `my employer is a public service body`
    `my employer is a public entity`
    `my employer is another employer`

DECLARE `Where to` IS ONE OF
    `to another public service body`
    `to a public entity`
    `to a different area of my own body or entity`

-- s 51(1): an employee of a public service body or public entity who has made a disclosure and believes on reasonable
-- grounds that detrimental action will be, is being or has been taken "may request a transfer": a grant limited by its
-- own wording, NOTHING outside it.
@export Can I ask to be transferred to protect me from reprisal (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 51(1))? An employee of a public service body or public entity who has made a public interest disclosure and believes on reasonable grounds that detrimental action will be, is being or has been taken against them may request a transfer.
GIVEN `who employs me` IS A `My employer` @desc Who employs you: a public service body or a public entity (within the meaning of the Public Administration Act 2004), or another employer
      `have I made a public interest disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made a public interest disclosure
      `do I believe on reasonable grounds I face reprisal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you believe, on reasonable grounds, that detrimental action will be, is being or has been taken against you in reprisal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I ask to be transferred` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`who employs me` EQUALS `my employer is another employer`)) AND `have I made a public interest disclosure` AND `do I believe on reasonable grounds I face reprisal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 51(1))

-- s 51(2): a public service body employee to another public service body, a public entity, or a different area of the
-- same body; (3): a public entity employee to a public service body or a different area of the same entity -- not to
-- another public entity (finding 10). (4) "may only be transferred under subsection (2) or (3) if" (a) to (d): JUST
-- FALSE where one fails, and for a destination (2) or (3) does not list (fork F13). Terms "no less favourable overall".
@export Can I be transferred there (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 51(2) to (6))? A public service body employee may be moved to another public service body, a public entity or another area of the same body; a public entity employee to a public service body or another area of the same entity. Only if you request or consent, your Head has reasonable grounds to suspect reprisal and considers the transfer will reduce the risk, the receiving Head consents, and the terms and conditions are no less favourable overall. The transfer is not a resignation or termination; your service is continuous.
GIVEN `who employs me` IS A `My employer` @desc Who employs you: a public service body, a public entity, or another employer
      `where to` IS A `Where to` @desc Where you would be transferred to
      `have I made a public interest disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made a public interest disclosure
      `did I request or consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you requested or consented to the transfer
      `does my Head suspect reprisal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Head of your public service body or public entity has reasonable grounds to suspect that detrimental action will be, is being or has been taken against you in contravention of s 45
      `does my Head consider it will reduce the risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your Head considers the transfer will avoid, reduce or eliminate the risk of detrimental action against you
      `does the receiving Head consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Head of the body or entity you would move to consents (answer yes for a move within your own body)
      `are the terms no less favourable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the terms and conditions of employment after the transfer are no less favourable overall
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be transferred there` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `who employs me` EQUALS `my employer is another employer` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 51(2), (3))
           IF `who employs me` EQUALS `my employer is a public entity` AND `where to` EQUALS `to a public entity` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE `as an answer` (    `have I made a public interest disclosure`
                                     AND `did I request or consent`
                                     AND `does my Head suspect reprisal`
                                     AND `does my Head consider it will reduce the risk`
                                     AND `does the receiving Head consent`
                                     AND `are the terms no less favourable`)

§§ `Confidentiality of my disclosure`

-- s 52(1) applies to the people listed; (2) "must not disclose"; (3) "does not apply if": the exceptions, JUST FALSE.
-- Outside (1) and for a disclosure that is not assessable: NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*.
@export Would it be an offence for this person to pass on the content of my disclosure (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 52)? A person or body to whom an assessable disclosure was made, or who received it in their duties, or was given its content by an integrity body for assessment, must not disclose its content (up to 120 penalty units or 12 months' imprisonment, or 600 penalty units for a body corporate), except in the circumstances of s 54, by direction of the investigating entity, as necessary for lawful action including discipline, after a determination that it is not a public interest complaint, or after it was lawfully published.
GIVEN `how did it reach the integrity bodies` IS A `How it reached the integrity bodies` @desc How your disclosure came to be an "assessable disclosure": made to the IBAC; to Integrity Oversight Victoria or the Integrity and Oversight Committee as s 14 requires; to another entity that must notify it for assessment (because it considers the disclosure may show improper conduct or reprisal); a police complaint disclosure; a related disclosure made in an investigation; or none of these
      `is the person one s 52 binds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person or body passing it on is one to whom the disclosure was made, who received it in their duties under the Act, who was given its content by the IBAC, Integrity Oversight Victoria or the Integrity and Oversight Committee for assessment, or who received it in an excepted or unlawful disclosure
      `why was it passed on` IS A `Why it was passed on` @desc The circumstance in which the content was passed on, or none of these
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Would passing on the content be an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `how did it reach the integrity bodies` EQUALS `none of these, so not an assessable disclosure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 52(1), "assessable disclosure")
           IF (NOT `is the person one s 52 binds`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 52(1))
           OTHERWISE `as an answer` (NOT (`s 52(3) -- an exception for the content` `why was it passed on`))

-- s 53(1) "must not disclose information likely to lead to the identification of a person who has made an assessable
-- disclosure"; (2) "does not apply if": the exceptions, JUST FALSE.
@export Would it be an offence for someone to pass on information likely to identify me as the person who made the disclosure (Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) s 53)? No person or body may disclose information likely to lead to your identification as the maker of an assessable disclosure (up to 120 penalty units or 12 months' imprisonment, or 600 penalty units for a body corporate), except with your written consent, in the circumstances of s 54, after a determination that it is not a public interest complaint, or after it was lawfully published.
GIVEN `how did it reach the integrity bodies` IS A `How it reached the integrity bodies` @desc How your disclosure came to be an "assessable disclosure" (see the content question), or none of these
      `why was it passed on` IS A `Why it was passed on` @desc The circumstance in which the information was passed on, or none of these
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Would identifying me be an offence` MEANS
    IF `how did it reach the integrity bodies` EQUALS `none of these, so not an assessable disclosure`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 53(1), "assessable disclosure")
    ELSE `as an answer` (NOT (`s 53(2) -- an exception for my identity` `why was it passed on`))

§§ `Offences and penalties`

@export What is the maximum fine, in penalty units, for an offence under the Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic)? Reprisal (s 45) 240 penalty units; disclosing the content of an assessable disclosure or information identifying the discloser (ss 52, 53) 120 for a person, 600 for a body corporate; false or misleading information and false claims (ss 72, 73) 120. The Act sets no separate figure for a body corporate under ss 45, 72 and 73 (no answer is given). The dollar value of a penalty unit is fixed each year under the Monetary Units Act 2004.
GIVEN `which offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence
      `is it a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offender is a body corporate (answer no for an individual)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the maximum fine in penalty units` MEANS `the maximum penalty units for` `which offence` `is it a body corporate`

@export What is the maximum term of imprisonment, in months, for an offence under the Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic)? Reprisal (s 45) 2 years; the confidentiality offences (ss 52, 53) and false information or claims (ss 72, 73) 12 months; each "or both" with the fine. None for a body corporate.
GIVEN `which offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence
      `is it a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offender is a body corporate
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS `the maximum months of imprisonment for` `which offence` `is it a body corporate`
